# Who reviews what. GitHub requests a review from the matching owners on
# every pull request, skipping the author. When several lines match a file,
# the LAST one wins, so general rules go first and overrides go below.
#
# Both of us are listed on every path on purpose: nobody can approve their
# own pull request, so a path with a single owner would block that owner's
# PRs once "Require review from Code Owners" is on. Listing both means the
# other person is always the one asked. Lead owner is named first.

# Default: anything not matched below (root README, docs/, archive/, .github/).
*            @joel-prashanth @Sai-Siv

